---
title: Pancakes
cooklang: 2
servings: 4
makes: about fourteen 4-inch cakes
source: Irma S. Rombauer and Marion Rombauer Becker, Joy of Cooking (1975 ed.)
course: breakfast
---

`Separate` @eggs{1-2}. -> yolks + whites

= Batter

`Sift together` @flour{1.5%cup}|(@flour{3%parts} + @cornmeal{1%part})[or buckwheat for the cornmeal],
@double-acting baking powder{1.75%tsp}, @sugar{3%tbsp} and @?salt{1%tsp} in a #mixing bowl{}. -> dry ingredients

`Mix` @milk{1.25%cups}, @melted butter{3%tbsp}|@canola oil{}[or another flavourless cooking oil] and the @&yolks{}. -> milk mixture

`Stir` the @&milk mixture{} into the @&dry ingredients{}, mixing thoroughly. -> batter

`Beat` the @&whites{} until ~{stiff}. -> beaten whites

`Fold` the @&beaten whites{} into the @&batter{} immediately before cooking.

`Fry` on a #griddle{} at medium heat.

> The salt can be left out at a minor expense of flavour.
